    "lastText": "The `minisheet` engine is built as specified in TASK.md. `npm test` runs 62 tests and all pass. Nothing is committed yet.\n\nFiles added:\n- `src/sheet.js`: the `Sheet` class, tokenizer, parser, evaluator, and all listed functions.\n- `test/sheet.test.js`: tests for literals, operators, coercion, errors, cycles, every function group, and a large sparse range.\n- `README.md`: API, operators, error rules, and the full function list.\n- `package.json`: `npm test` runs `node --test`. No dependencies.\n\nJudgment calls where TASK.md is silent or ambiguous:\n- **Cycles:** every cell in a cycle, and every cell that depends on one, is `#CIRC!`. `IFERROR` does not hide a cycle, since the spec says every cell in the chain must be `#CIRC!`.\n- **`COUNT`:** text that can't be coerced to a number is skipped rather than giving `#VALUE!`. Errors still propagate.\n- **Error order in ranges:** the first error is taken row by row, with arguments in order.\n- **Criteria functions:** errors in the criteria range propagate, which follows the general rule. Errors in the sum or average range only propagate when that cell is matched.\n- **Empty-cell criteria:** blank cells match `<>` criteria, as in common spreadsheets.\n- **`MATCH`:** a scalar argument or a two-dimensional range gives `#VALUE!`.\n- **Boolean literals:** `TRUE`/`FALSE` are recognized in any case without trimming, so `\" TRUE \"` stays text. Numeric literals do accept surrounding spaces.\n\nKnown limits:\n- Recalculation clears the whole value cache on every `set`, then computes lazily. Correct, but not incremental.\n- Deep dependency chains recurse, so very long chains could exhaust the JS stack. I did not test this limit.\n\nI have not committed. Say if you want a commit on `master`, or a branch and PR.",
